## 7. Caching

*(Full treatment: `BackendForAi.md` Ch 17.)* The system-design framing:

```
 In a normal backend, caching saves MILLISECONDS.
 In an AI backend, caching saves SECONDS AND MONEY.

 A 30% hit rate on a $50,000/month inference bill is $15,000/month,
 recovered by a component you build in an afternoon. Nothing else in
 this phase has that return.
```

```
 THE FOUR CACHES, BY VALUE
 ① PROVIDER PREFIX CACHE   stable content first in the prompt → ~10× cheaper
                           prefix. Pure reordering. Do this first.
 ② EMBEDDING CACHE         deterministic, never invalidates, 40–70% hit rate
 ③ RETRIEVAL CACHE         keyed by query hash + corpus version
 ④ RESPONSE CACHE          exact-match at temperature 0 only; semantic
                           caching at ≥0.95 similarity, tenant-scoped

 THE THREE FAILURE MODES
   STAMPEDE      hot key expires, 1,000 concurrent misses hammer the source
                 → single-flight lock (SET NX) + stale-while-revalidate
   PENETRATION   requests for keys that don't exist always miss
                 → cache negative results briefly
   AVALANCHE     many keys written together expire together
                 → jitter every TTL

 ⚠ EVERY CACHE KEY NEEDS THE TENANT ID. A cache lookup bypasses every
   authorization check you wrote.
```

