## Checklist

```
ARCHITECTURE
[ ] Modular monolith unless a concrete split reason exists
[ ] API / inference / worker tiers separated (different scaling + hardware)
[ ] URL space grouped by domain so extraction is a routing change
[ ] Gateway does generic HTTP hygiene; app does identity-aware policy

MESSAGING
[ ] Queue chosen by need, not fashion (Redis Streams is usually enough)
[ ] Every task idempotent (status guard, stable IDs, upsert, idem keys)
[ ] Outbox pattern wherever a DB write and an enqueue must agree
[ ] Bounded retries + DLQ + alerting + a replay path

RESILIENCE
[ ] Retry at ONE layer, with full jitter and a total-time cap
[ ] Circuit breaker per external dependency, with metrics
[ ] Timeout budgets decreasing inward
[ ] Bounded queues and semaphores on every fan-out
[ ] Degradation ladder decided per dependency, and tested in a game day
[ ] Multiple LLM providers configured

SCALE
[ ] Stateless services; no model in the API process
[ ] Least-connections + HTTP/2 for streaming
[ ] Connection pool arithmetic verified against max_connections
[ ] Vector search on a read replica once volume is real
[ ] Four rate-limit layers including a GLOBAL spend ceiling

CONSISTENCY
[ ] Consistency requirement chosen per data type, not globally
[ ] No distributed transactions; outbox or saga instead
[ ] Locks only where atomic operations can't do the job; CAS release

OBSERVABILITY
[ ] Request ID at the edge, propagated, returned, on every log line
[ ] Cost per request logged and alerted on
[ ] Traces sampled at 10%, forced at 100% on errors
[ ] Alerts on user-visible symptoms, each with a runbook
```

